---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout 
  title="About the Engine | EV Kelly Calculator"
  description="The mathematical methodology, privacy architecture, and engineering behind the EV Kelly position sizing calculator."
>
  <div class="max-w-[900px] mx-auto w-full min-h-screen px-4 py-12 md:py-20 flex flex-col">
    
    <header class="flex flex-col items-center text-center mx-auto mb-16 max-w-3xl">
      <h1 class="animate-reveal text-5xl sm:text-6xl md:text-7xl font-bold tracking-tighter text-[var(--theme-text-main)] mb-6 leading-tight" style="opacity: 0;">
        About The Engine
      </h1>
      <p class="animate-reveal delay-100 text-lg sm:text-xl text-[var(--theme-text-muted)] font-medium leading-relaxed" style="opacity: 0;">
        Built to solve a single mathematical problem: stopping algorithmic traders from blowing up their accounts.
      </p>
    </header>

    <div class="animate-reveal delay-200 flex flex-col gap-8 w-full" style="opacity: 0;">
      
      <section class="liquid-panel static-panel w-full px-8 pb-8 md:px-10 md:pb-10 pt-0 flex flex-col items-center text-center border border-white/[0.12] shadow-[inset_0_1px_1px_rgba(255,255,255,0.05)]">
        <div class="w-full border-b border-[var(--liquid-input-border)] py-8 md:py-10 mb-6">
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-white tracking-tight m-0 leading-none">
            The Retail Variance Trap
          </h2>
        </div>
        <p class="text-base text-[var(--theme-text-muted)] leading-relaxed">
          Traders spend years hunting for the perfect entry signal, only to lose everything in a week because of terrible risk management. A trading edge is completely useless if your position sizing guarantees you won't survive a normal losing streak. This calculator was built to replace emotional gambling with hard, mathematical capital allocation.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="liquid-panel static-panel w-full px-8 pb-8 md:px-10 md:pb-10 pt-0 flex flex-col items-center text-center border border-white/[0.12] shadow-[inset_0_1px_1px_rgba(255,255,255,0.05)]">
        <div class="w-full border-b border-[var(--liquid-input-border)] py-8 md:py-10 mb-6">
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-white tracking-tight m-0 leading-none">
            Quantitative Methodology
          </h2>
        </div>
        <p class="text-base text-[var(--theme-text-muted)] leading-relaxed">
          There are no magic indicators here. The engine is built strictly on the Kelly Criterion—the mathematical formula used by quantitative funds to maximize compound growth while mathematically capping the Risk of Ruin. By utilizing Full, Half, or Quarter Kelly outputs, you can scale your risk exactly to your system's proven edge.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="liquid-panel static-panel w-full px-8 pb-8 md:px-10 md:pb-10 pt-0 flex flex-col items-center text-center border border-white/[0.12] shadow-[inset_0_1px_1px_rgba(255,255,255,0.05)]">
        <div class="w-full border-b border-[var(--liquid-input-border)] py-8 md:py-10 mb-6">
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-white tracking-tight m-0 leading-none">
            Client-Side Data Architecture
          </h2>
        </div>
        <p class="text-base text-[var(--theme-text-muted)] leading-relaxed">
          Your trading data is your edge. The EV Kelly engine runs entirely client-side within your web browser. There is no backend database storing your inputs, win rates, or bankroll size. Everything you calculate remains completely private, secure, and isolated to your local machine.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="liquid-panel static-panel w-full px-8 pb-8 md:px-10 md:pb-10 pt-0 flex flex-col items-center text-center border border-white/[0.12] shadow-[inset_0_1px_1px_rgba(255,255,255,0.05)]">
        <div class="w-full border-b border-[var(--liquid-input-border)] py-8 md:py-10 mb-6">
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-white tracking-tight m-0 leading-none">
            The Developer
          </h2>
        </div>
        <p class="text-base text-[var(--theme-text-muted)] leading-relaxed mb-4">
          The EV Kelly engine is engineered and maintained by Rahul Yadranvi. With a specialized background in modern full-stack web development (Next.js, TypeScript), the platform was built to bridge the gap between complex quantitative models and accessible retail tools. The architecture reflects a commitment to mathematical reality, institutional-grade design, and zero-compromise data privacy.
        </p>
        <div class="flex gap-4 mt-2 justify-center">
          <a href="https://github.com/RahulYadranvi" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="text-sm font-bold text-[var(--theme-accent-blue)] hover:text-white transition-colors">
            View GitHub Profile &rarr;
          </a>
          <a href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/rahulyadranvi/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="text-sm font-bold text-[var(--theme-accent-blue)] hover:text-white transition-colors">
            View LinkedIn &rarr;
          </a>
        </div>
      </section>

    </div>
  </div>
</Layout>

<script type="application/ld+json" is:inline>
{
  "@context": "https://schema.org",
  "@type": "Person",
  "name": "Rahul Yadranvi",
  "url": "https://evkellycalc.com/about",
  "jobTitle": "Full-Stack Software Engineer",
  "sameAs": [
    "https://github.com/RahulYadranvi",
    "https://www.linkedin.com/in/rahulyadranvi/"
  ]
}
</script>